 ## Overview
-CLA-NeRF is a differentiable representation for articulated objects that explicitly models part and joint attributes, disentangling camera pose, part pose, part segmentation, and joint attributes to allow independent control during rendering [S1]. It solves the problem of rendering deformable articulated objects at unseen poses and estimating their articulated pose from RGB images, without requiring CAD models or depth data [S1]. Unlike standard NeRF formulations which model camera poses but ignore object articulation, CLA-NeRF predicts a part segmentation field alongside density and color, enabling the inference of joint attributes via line-fitting on the segmentation field [S1]. It differs from sibling methods like NARF by focusing on general articulated objects without assuming known joint attributes (e.g., bone length) at test time, and by using part segmentation labels for supervision rather than explicit joint attributes [S1].
+CLA-NeRF is a differentiable representation for articulated objects that explicitly models part and joint attributes, disentangling camera pose, part pose, part segmentation, and joint attributes to allow independent control during rendering [S1]. It solves the problem of rendering deformable articulated objects at unseen poses and estimating their articulated pose from RGB images, without requiring CAD models or depth data [S1]. Unlike standard NeRF formulations which model camera poses but ignore object articulation, CLA-NeRF predicts a part segmentation field alongside density and color, enabling the inference of joint attributes via line-fitting on the segmentation field [S1]. It differs from sibling methods like [MoCo-NeRF](16197-moco-nerf.md), [A-NeRF](18108-a-nerf.md), [SelfNeRF](18160-selfnerf.md), and [NARF](18108-a-nerf.md) by focusing on general articulated objects without assuming known joint attributes (e.g., bone length) at test time, and by using part segmentation labels for supervision rather than explicit joint attributes [S1].
 
